1
00:00:00,367 --> 00:00:02,067
Just because Serizawa ate those snacks,

2
00:00:02,167 --> 00:00:04,900
he was asked to go on a date.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,600
A date...?

4
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:10,733
Do you want to try going on a date with me?

5
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,000
Huh?

6
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,367
A what?

7
00:00:14,567 --> 00:00:15,800
A date.

8
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:18,833
Isn't this the exact place in
"Deep Sea and Starry Sky"

9
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:21,033
where Hasefuka had his first date?!

10
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:24,967
No, it should be like this.

11
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:26,967
Wouldn't this make us...

12
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:29,300
just like a real couple?

13
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,267
For someone like me

14
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,600
to be hanging out with Serizawa...

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,767
I feel a bit self-conscious.

16
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:38,533
Suzuki, you're selling
yourself way too short.

17
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:40,467
Huh?

18
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:42,267
You're really cute, Suzuki.

19
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:45,833
You're the number one
person I want to be with.

20
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:49,067
Stop it, stop it.

21
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,367
Aren't you going to write it, Suzuki?

22
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:56,367
The kissing scene.

23
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:58,467
Ah...

24
00:00:59,167 --> 00:01:00,633
I was planning to write it.

25
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:02,433
Right at the end of the date scene.

26
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:04,267
Suzuki.

27
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,867
Look at me.

28
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,167
When it comes to Serizawa...

29
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,467
I really only feel one way.

30
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:46,467
I like you.

31
00:02:06,933 --> 00:02:08,367
Suzuki.

32
00:02:09,567 --> 00:02:10,933
I...

33
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:13,333
Wait a minute!

34
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:14,600
Hmm?

35
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,133
What exactly are we doing?

36
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:18,333
What do you mean... kissing?

37
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:20,167
I'm sorry.

38
00:02:20,267 --> 00:02:21,267
Don't apologize.

39
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,867
No, I mean, we really shouldn't be kissing.

40
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,833
What... what should we do?

41
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Calm down.

42
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,367
Wait, that's not it.

43
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:30,500
I know, even if we call it a kiss,

44
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,433
it's just for research and practice.

45
00:02:32,533 --> 00:02:34,933
That's exactly why we can't actually do it!

46
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:36,333
What on earth am I doing?

47
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,640
Calm down, you need to calm down.

48
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:39,133
How could I possibly calm down?

49
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:42,300
Besides... that would be my first kiss.

50
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:46,533
Oh, so I'd be your first.

51
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:48,600
Serizawa, wipe that smirk off your face!

52
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:49,800
Ah, sorry, sorry.

53
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:53,033
Anyway, how are you so
calm about this, Serizawa?

54
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,200
Well...

55
00:02:57,067 --> 00:02:58,109
Suzuki...

56
00:02:58,133 --> 00:02:59,667
Forget about it.

57
00:02:59,767 --> 00:03:02,767
Yeah, that's for the best. Let's do that.

58
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:03,700
Huh?

59
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,300
One, two, clear your mind!

60
00:03:06,767 --> 00:03:07,400
You forgot it.

61
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,333
You forgot, right?

62
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,120
Yeah, I forgot.

63
00:03:11,133 --> 00:03:12,176
Like I could ever forget that easily!

64
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,700
Anyway, thanks so much for today.

65
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,133
See you at school. I'm heading off.

66
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:28,467
I have to forget...

67
00:03:28,567 --> 00:03:30,267
Forget it.

68
00:03:30,367 --> 00:03:33,867
Ah... forget it.

69
00:03:58,133 --> 00:04:03,133
How could I possibly forget?!

70
00:04:50,867 --> 00:04:53,833
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

71
00:04:55,667 --> 00:04:59,433
(Episode 6)

72
00:04:59,533 --> 00:05:01,200
I really need to forget it...

73
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,167
I seriously have to forget...

74
00:05:03,267 --> 00:05:04,433
Good morning...

75
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:09,300
Gotta forget...

76
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:19,500
Anyway, just act normal. Stay calm...

77
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:21,533
Okay.

78
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:24,167
Good morning, Teacher Suzuki.

79
00:05:24,267 --> 00:05:26,500
G-Good morning.

80
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:28,667
You're stuttering way too much.

81
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:31,800
No, I just can't do it.

82
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,767
I can't even look him in the eye.

83
00:05:34,733 --> 00:05:37,467
By the way, Suzuki, aren't you wearing it?

84
00:05:41,167 --> 00:05:42,733
Ah... yeah.

85
00:05:43,033 --> 00:05:44,767
Sorry, I forgot.

86
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,600
Morning.

87
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,133
W-What?

88
00:05:54,833 --> 00:05:55,933
Nothing.

89
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:02,300
Just thinking about how fun yesterday was.

90
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,300
Morning.

91
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,567
Good morning.

92
00:06:06,367 --> 00:06:07,467
So, how was it?

93
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:08,867
What did you guys do yesterday?

94
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,933
Ah, well...

95
00:06:12,033 --> 00:06:13,067
A date.

96
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,476
- Wait... A date?
- Didn't we agree to forget about it?

97
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:19,000
Ah, no, well... we just went
out to research a date scene.

98
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,467
That's why we hung out for a bit.

99
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:24,333
Oh, for your novel.

100
00:06:25,267 --> 00:06:27,767
I see. So what did you guys do?

101
00:06:28,333 --> 00:06:32,900
We went to the aquarium to see
the fish, hit up some photo spots,

102
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,967
grabbed some tea, and then...

103
00:06:36,067 --> 00:06:38,600
And then we k-k...

104
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,133
Hey, what are you doing...

105
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,533
K-K...?

106
00:06:42,667 --> 00:06:44,033
Keychains! We bought keychains.

107
00:06:45,167 --> 00:06:47,667
Ah, so that's what it is...

108
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,900
Keychains, oh, those?

109
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,300
- Wow.
- The color is so dark.

110
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:59,086
What do you mean,
"so that's what it is..."?

111
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,133
Ah... nothing.

112
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:11,067
Am I overthinking this?

113
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:21,067
I feel like Serizawa is
acting a bit different today.

114
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,867
Where are you going?

115
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:15,033
To the b-bathroom.

116
00:08:15,733 --> 00:08:16,767
I'll go too.

117
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:18,700
Eh...

118
00:08:20,767 --> 00:08:24,767
Serizawa has been acting
a bit weird lately anyway,

119
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:37,567
but he feels super intense today.

120
00:08:43,667 --> 00:08:46,533
Isn't the distance between those two
a bit weird today?

121
00:08:49,067 --> 00:08:50,133
You think so?

122
00:08:50,233 --> 00:08:51,700
No, it's definitely weird.

123
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:52,833
Huh?

124
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:54,067
Huh?

125
00:08:54,733 --> 00:08:56,533
- What's weird about it?
- Look.

126
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,367
- Hey, wait a sec...
- W-What?

127
00:09:00,467 --> 00:09:02,267
Huh? Was that fried chicken just now?

128
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:03,533
You're acting weird too.

129
00:09:03,633 --> 00:09:04,900
Why?

130
00:09:28,567 --> 00:09:29,967
Um, Suzuki.

131
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,000
W-What?

132
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,067
K-K...

133
00:09:33,167 --> 00:09:34,733
What? Are you extorting him?

134
00:09:35,133 --> 00:09:38,467
Serizawa, you're making
Suzuki uncomfortable.

135
00:09:39,167 --> 00:09:41,867
Come on, Suzuki, over here.

136
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,000
What's your problem?

137
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:48,100
I didn't even do anything.

138
00:09:50,933 --> 00:09:52,000
Whatever.

139
00:09:55,033 --> 00:09:58,667
That guy is in a bad mood today.

140
00:10:10,767 --> 00:10:13,233
Isn't Serizawa acting a bit weird today?

141
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:15,800
He seems unusually quiet.

142
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:18,867
He looks so cool when he's not talking.

143
00:10:18,967 --> 00:10:19,833
That's hilarious.

144
00:10:19,933 --> 00:10:21,243
Yeah, maybe he's at his best like this.

145
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:21,800
Huh?

146
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,233
- Ah, Yuma is still number one.
- Huh?

147
00:10:24,333 --> 00:10:26,033
Yep, number one.

148
00:10:26,533 --> 00:10:31,333
Is he still mad about yesterday?

149
00:10:32,167 --> 00:10:33,700
- Suzuki.
- Hmm?

150
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:39,267
Did something happen between
you and Serizawa yesterday?

151
00:10:40,067 --> 00:10:42,533
Ah, no.

152
00:10:46,173 --> 00:10:47,373
No!

153
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,800
Nothing, really nothing happened.

154
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,967
Nothing at all?

155
00:10:54,533 --> 00:10:56,200
I can't keep thinking about it.

156
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,300
Anyway, that whole kissing thing...

157
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,500
I need to completely erase
it from my mind right now.

158
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:08,300
What were you guys just talking about?

159
00:11:12,167 --> 00:11:14,967
Nothing, we weren't talking about anything.

160
00:11:16,233 --> 00:11:17,467
I see.

161
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:22,933
Suzuki, about yesterday...

162
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:25,033
Is there anything you want to tell me?

163
00:11:29,733 --> 00:11:30,900
Yesterday?

164
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:32,900
Yeah... go on.

165
00:11:38,467 --> 00:11:40,100
Yesterday was fun, right?

166
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,400
Look, there were so many
fish at the aquarium too.

167
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,967
Ah, right, Teacher Usami is looking for me.

168
00:11:45,067 --> 00:11:46,067
I gotta go.

169
00:11:47,433 --> 00:11:48,900
What is up with you guys?

170
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,300
I told you, it's nothing.

171
00:12:01,933 --> 00:12:03,467
What am I supposed to do?

172
00:12:09,867 --> 00:12:11,033
Whoa!

173
00:12:15,133 --> 00:12:16,367
Suzuki!

174
00:12:33,167 --> 00:12:34,333
I'm sorry!

175
00:12:49,033 --> 00:12:50,733
Heave-ho.

176
00:12:50,833 --> 00:12:52,100
What are we doing today?

177
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:54,700
Then it's decided.

178
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,100
Let's go to karaoke.

179
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:56,633
- Karaoke?
- Yeah.

180
00:12:56,733 --> 00:12:58,667
- I can't wait.
- Serizawa, you...

181
00:12:59,467 --> 00:13:01,133
- Serizawa.
- Hey.

182
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:03,733
What?

183
00:13:03,967 --> 00:13:05,067
Huh?

184
00:13:30,033 --> 00:13:31,367
What should I do?

185
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,067
If this keeps up,

186
00:13:33,167 --> 00:13:36,033
I won't even be able to talk to Serizawa...

187
00:13:36,533 --> 00:13:37,867
Alright.

188
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,800
It's fine, isn't it?

189
00:13:40,267 --> 00:13:41,433
Serizawa.

190
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,733
L-Let's just drop this for now.

191
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:52,633
Does this mean we can
never laugh together again?

192
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:57,167
Suzuki?

193
00:13:58,267 --> 00:13:59,700
What are you doing?

194
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,400
Ah, well...

195
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,100
Ah, right, are you free today?

196
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,640
Do you want to grab a bite together?

197
00:14:05,900 --> 00:14:07,600
Huh, ah...

198
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:09,600
Yeah.

199
00:14:10,633 --> 00:14:12,267
Suzuki says he can come.

200
00:14:13,433 --> 00:14:15,200
Got it!

201
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,100
Awesome.

202
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:18,900
I'm so happy!

203
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,109
- I'm seriously so happy.
- You're so loud.

204
00:14:20,133 --> 00:14:22,143
You've been saying you wanted
to go with everyone for a while now.

205
00:14:22,167 --> 00:14:24,276
- Yeah, yeah, I've been talking about it non-stop.
- Shut up.

206
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,433
- I'm just super hyped!
- That's enough.

207
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:28,433
You're actually secretly
thrilled, aren't you?

208
00:14:28,733 --> 00:14:30,133
You're so annoying.

209
00:14:30,219 --> 00:14:33,086
(Banana Lake)

210
00:14:37,367 --> 00:14:42,333
All right, let's start the
homeroom meeting.

211
00:14:42,433 --> 00:14:43,567
Looking forward to it.

212
00:14:43,667 --> 00:14:45,100
Looking forward to it.

213
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,233
Homeroom meeting?

214
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:50,533
The agenda is "The awkward
vibe between Serizawa and Suzuki."

215
00:14:50,633 --> 00:14:51,643
That's a ridiculous agenda.

216
00:14:51,667 --> 00:14:53,633
It's fine, it's fine.

217
00:14:53,733 --> 00:14:54,467
Are you sure about this?

218
00:14:54,567 --> 00:14:56,267
Takeuchi is in charge of taking notes.

219
00:14:56,367 --> 00:14:57,367
Happy to help.

220
00:14:57,391 --> 00:15:00,091
Iwasaki is on peacemaker duty.

221
00:15:01,867 --> 00:15:03,233
Leave it to me.

222
00:15:03,333 --> 00:15:04,467
Who's going to fight?

223
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:06,933
Then I'll just ask straight out.

224
00:15:07,033 --> 00:15:08,533
What exactly is going on?

225
00:15:14,567 --> 00:15:15,933
I refuse to answer.

226
00:15:16,667 --> 00:15:20,267
Did something happen
between you two at the aquarium?

227
00:15:20,367 --> 00:15:24,533
Just confess already. You'll
feel better once you say it.

228
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:26,400
What exactly happened?

229
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,033
Hey.

230
00:15:29,267 --> 00:15:32,433
Can I really say it?

231
00:15:32,533 --> 00:15:33,600
Sure.

232
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:41,900
Actually, Serizawa and I...

233
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,400
K-

234
00:15:48,633 --> 00:15:51,367
K-

235
00:15:51,467 --> 00:15:52,467
Kissed.

236
00:15:52,533 --> 00:15:53,533
Huh?

237
00:15:53,567 --> 00:15:54,767
Kissed?

238
00:15:57,467 --> 00:15:59,267
So you two kissed?

239
00:16:03,067 --> 00:16:04,067
That's it?

240
00:16:04,133 --> 00:16:06,433
What the heck, it was just a kiss.

241
00:16:06,767 --> 00:16:08,076
Meeting adjourned, meeting adjourned.

242
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:08,933
Good work, everyone.

243
00:16:09,033 --> 00:16:10,400
- Good work.
- Court dismissed.

244
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:11,676
- Good work.
- Hold on a second.

245
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:13,267
- Wh-What is it?
- Excuse me.

246
00:16:13,367 --> 00:16:15,000
What are you doing? Stop it.

247
00:16:15,333 --> 00:16:16,733
Cut it out.

248
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,967
- Huh?
- Should we take this outside?

249
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:21,367
- No way.
- Are we really going outside?

250
00:16:21,467 --> 00:16:23,633
- Hey.
- That's enough.

251
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:25,067
Um, Serizawa.

252
00:16:28,867 --> 00:16:30,133
I'm really sorry.

253
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:33,633
It's all my fault.

254
00:16:33,733 --> 00:16:35,493
That's why things got
so awkward between us.

255
00:16:37,167 --> 00:16:42,900
Um, if it's okay with you...

256
00:16:45,467 --> 00:16:49,367
If you don't hate me...

257
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:59,267
I want us to... make up.

258
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,767
What the heck is this?

259
00:17:07,633 --> 00:17:10,500
You're making me look so lame.

260
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:13,833
No way, you're super cool, Serizawa.

261
00:17:13,933 --> 00:17:15,833
Besides, you've looked in a mirror, right?

262
00:17:17,933 --> 00:17:19,900
No, that's not what I mean.

263
00:17:25,467 --> 00:17:26,800
At the end of the day...

264
00:17:27,167 --> 00:17:31,100
I never thought Suzuki and I were fighting.

265
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:35,767
And I didn't think things were
awkward between us either.

266
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,467
Oh, really?

267
00:17:41,133 --> 00:17:42,333
Yeah.

268
00:17:42,433 --> 00:17:44,333
Suzuki didn't do anything wrong.

269
00:17:44,967 --> 00:17:48,767
I was just rushing things.

270
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,733
That's why I acted a bit weird.

271
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,533
Sorry.

272
00:17:58,733 --> 00:18:00,200
No.

273
00:18:00,933 --> 00:18:02,400
I'm the one who should apologize.

274
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:04,300
You don't need to apologize.

275
00:18:06,467 --> 00:18:12,067
I'll match your pace from now on.

276
00:18:17,067 --> 00:18:18,400
Thanks.

277
00:18:20,633 --> 00:18:21,833
Huh?

278
00:18:22,167 --> 00:18:23,167
Pace?

279
00:18:23,267 --> 00:18:28,133
So that's how it is, Serizawa.

280
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,067
Oh, I see.

281
00:18:30,967 --> 00:18:32,467
So that's what's going on.

282
00:18:32,867 --> 00:18:36,033
I kind of guessed it already, though.

283
00:18:36,133 --> 00:18:38,033
But you're being way too aggressive.

284
00:18:38,133 --> 00:18:40,533
Yeah, that's pushing it a bit too far.

285
00:18:40,633 --> 00:18:41,533
Shut up.

286
00:18:41,633 --> 00:18:43,133
I know that already.

287
00:18:43,733 --> 00:18:46,300
What have you guys been
talking about this whole time?

288
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,700
It's nothing, Suzuki. Don't worry about it.

289
00:18:51,367 --> 00:18:52,633
It's nothing.

290
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:53,800
What do you mean, nothing?

291
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,600
Nothing, nothing.

292
00:18:56,433 --> 00:18:57,233
But...

293
00:18:57,333 --> 00:18:59,367
We said it's nothing.

294
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,100
What does that even mean?

295
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,760
One, two, three, four, three, two, one.

296
00:19:02,833 --> 00:19:03,833
Serizawa!

297
00:19:03,867 --> 00:19:05,033
- Boom, boom.
- Oh.

298
00:19:05,133 --> 00:19:06,167
Suzuki!

299
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:06,867
Doo-roo, doo-roo.

300
00:19:06,967 --> 00:19:08,467
It's nothing.

301
00:19:08,567 --> 00:19:09,700
Oh.

302
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:12,033
I'm hungry.

303
00:19:12,133 --> 00:19:13,533
Eat as much as you want.

304
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:23,267
Thank goodness. I finally
made up with Serizawa.

305
00:19:24,067 --> 00:19:26,100
I told you we weren't fighting.

306
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:29,367
True, but I was really anxious.

307
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:34,333
I thought I'd never be able to
act like we usually do

308
00:19:34,433 --> 00:19:36,367
and chat happily with you again.

309
00:19:37,733 --> 00:19:39,233
I'm sorry, Suzuki.

310
00:19:41,233 --> 00:19:45,167
I'll never make you feel that way again.

311
00:19:46,267 --> 00:19:51,200
I won't make you anxious or
put you in a tough spot anymore.

312
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:54,433
About that kiss...

313
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:58,767
If it makes you uncomfortable,
you can just forget it ever happened.

314
00:20:04,467 --> 00:20:07,167
Actually, I'd rather not forget it.

315
00:20:09,467 --> 00:20:12,167
Let's just leave it. To me,

316
00:20:12,267 --> 00:20:17,833
all my memories with
you are precious treasures.

317
00:20:19,067 --> 00:20:21,500
I don't want to pretend it never happened.

318
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,600
Besides, that kiss...

319
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:28,833
You only kissed me because
you were looking out for me, right?

320
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,300
So I could keep writing my novel.

321
00:20:34,533 --> 00:20:35,693
Oh, so that's what you meant.

322
00:20:36,833 --> 00:20:38,376
What do you mean, "that's what you meant"?

323
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,200
No, it's nothing.

324
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:58,800
So I guess you don't need to yell "One,
two, clear your mind!" anymore, right?

325
00:20:59,467 --> 00:21:02,800
U-Um, I'm sorry about that, Serizawa.

326
00:21:03,433 --> 00:21:04,567
It's fine.

327
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:08,000
I won't forget it anyway.
I never planned to.

328
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:13,533
Or do you want to kiss again?

329
00:21:14,333 --> 00:21:15,467
Kiss?

330
00:21:15,567 --> 00:21:16,767
Huh?

331
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:17,967
Idiot!

332
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:20,833
No, wait, you're not an idiot, Serizawa.

333
00:21:22,167 --> 00:21:23,600
What the heck?

334
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:25,667
Ah, just forget it.

335
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:28,033
One, two, clear your mind!

336
00:21:28,133 --> 00:21:30,967
Just forget about that.
Don't remember that part.

337
00:21:31,067 --> 00:21:33,000
I do want to cherish my memories with you,

338
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,109
but please just
forget that one thing.

339
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:35,433
Got it, got it. I'll forget it.

340
00:21:35,533 --> 00:21:36,433
Mind cleared!

341
00:21:36,533 --> 00:21:37,533
Completely forgotten.

342
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:14,800
- So cute.
- Thanks.

343
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:17,333
- You look so elegant.
- Not at all.

344
00:22:17,667 --> 00:22:19,067
How are things going?

345
00:22:19,167 --> 00:22:20,000
- Huh?
- What things?

346
00:22:20,100 --> 00:22:21,833
Your date with Serizawa.

347
00:22:21,933 --> 00:22:23,800
Oh, right.

348
00:22:24,900 --> 00:22:26,700
Actually, I didn't end up going.

349
00:22:27,133 --> 00:22:28,167
- Huh?
- Why not?

350
00:22:28,267 --> 00:22:29,600
He turned me down.

351
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,767
What? Why?

352
00:22:34,433 --> 00:22:37,667
Serizawa said he already likes someone.

353
00:22:37,767 --> 00:22:39,267
- Huh?
- He does?

354
00:22:39,367 --> 00:22:40,943
- Serizawa likes someone?
- You're kidding, right?

355
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:43,500
I heard he's had an unrequited
crush since freshman year.

356
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:46,233
Wow, he's so devoted.

357
00:22:46,333 --> 00:22:47,100
Hey, hey.

358
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:50,533
- He's so devoted.
- I know, right?

359
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:58,400
Serizawa has... someone he likes?

360
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:00,800
(Next Episode Preview)

361
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:03,467
Don't scare him, and don't startle him.

362
00:23:03,567 --> 00:23:04,267
Just approach him slowly.

363
00:23:04,367 --> 00:23:05,409
Want to walk home together?

364
00:23:05,433 --> 00:23:06,433
It can't be helped.

365
00:23:06,533 --> 00:23:08,700
You don't need a reason to like someone.

366
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,567
- All right!
- Here I go.

367
00:23:10,667 --> 00:23:11,707
Making a face like that...

368
00:23:11,733 --> 00:23:12,733
That's just too cute.

369
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:13,876
(This drama is purely fictional)

370
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:14,900
What are you doing?
